{
  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "The best configuration so far (config_038: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc 0.725) establishes that scvi_n200 is the dominant factor over scgpt (0.54), and transformer+weighted is the best aggregation/fusion combo. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) meaningfully contributes to performance with the best RNA encoder. Config_045 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) isolates this variable while keeping all other settings at their known-best values. If resnet50 performs within ~1-2% of 0.725, it offers a cheaper alternative; if it drops significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential and we should lock in the current best. This is the highest-information experiment among remaining options: it tests an unexplored axis (image encoder) with the strongest RNA encoder, rather than testing a likely-inferior RNA encoder (pca_n2000) or a combination of individually-worse choices (avgpool+concat in config_040). Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low, roughly 2.5–3.5 GPU hours, since resnet50 is substantially smaller than ViT-L, making this cheaper than config_038 (3.60 hrs) while retaining the transformer aggregation overhead."
}

